// MCF OVERRIDE of the vanilla character root, GUID {37578B1666981FCE}.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Talking to people has to work on the people already in
// a mission -- placed by a mission maker, spawned by an ambient system, part of
// a composition, or belonging to a modded faction MCF has never heard of. A
// dedicated MCF civilian prefab would only ever make MCF's own civilians
// talkable, which is close to useless.
//
// Every character in the game inherits from this one file, vanilla and modded
// alike, so this is the only place that reaches all of them.
//
// WHY IT IS A FULL COPY. A GUID override REPLACES a prefab; it does not merge
// with it. Measured, not assumed: vanilla EditorModeEdit.et is 16.4 KB and
// MCF's override of it is 17.0 KB -- a whole copy plus additions. So this file
// must carry everything vanilla's Character_Base carried.
//
// HOW IT WAS MADE, AND HOW TO REMAKE IT. Generated mechanically, never typed:
// the vanilla file was extracted from the game paks with game_duplicate, the
// MCF block below was inserted, and the result was written here with vanilla's
// own GUID in the .meta. Re-run those three steps after a game update. That
// matters, because this copy goes stale SILENTLY -- characters would simply
// keep the old values, with nothing in any log to say why.
//
// KNOWN CONFLICT. Any other mod that also overrides Character_Base will fight
// with this one; last loaded wins. That is the price of reaching every faction,
// and it was chosen deliberately over per-faction overrides, which cannot reach
// modded factions at all.
//
// WHAT MCF ADDS, AND WHY AN UNTOUCHED MISSION IS UNAFFECTED: a dialogue
// component with no nodes, a disposition component, and one talk action.
// MCF_Dialogue_Component.HasConversation() is false while nothing is authored,
// and the action hides itself in that case -- so no prompt appears on anybody
// until a conversation is actually assigned.
//
// EVERYTHING BELOW IS VANILLA, VERBATIM, EXCEPT the MCF_ entries.

